    doc.append('### Principles of Surgery-Based Intraoperative Transesophageal Echocardiography')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('Intraoperative transesophageal echocardiography (TEE) is an indispensable diagnostic and monitoring modality in modern cardiovascular surgery. It transforms perioperative care from passive observational hemodynamic monitoring into active, real-time surgical guidance across the full continuum of open, minimally invasive, robotic, and hybrid cardiovascular procedures:')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('1. **The Dual Phases of Intraoperative TEE:**')
    doc.append('   - **Pre-Cardiopulmonary Bypass (Pre-CPB) Evaluation:** Establishes baseline cardiac anatomy and hemodynamics under general anesthesia, confirms or refines the preoperative diagnosis, identifies unexpected secondary or incidental pathology (e.g., patent foramen ovale, ascending aortic atheroma, unsuspected valve regurgitation), determines surgical feasibility (e.g., valve repairability vs replacement), and guides vascular cannulation strategies.')
    doc.append('   - **Post-Cardiopulmonary Bypass (Post-CPB) Evaluation:** Assesses immediate surgical adequacy (residual regurgitation or stenosis, prosthetic valve seating, ventricular assist device cannula position, de-airing thoroughness), monitors regional and global biventricular performance during weaning from extracorporeal circulation, detects iatrogenic surgical complications (circumflex coronary artery distortion, aortic dissection, paravalvular leak, left ventricular outflow tract obstruction), and directs post-bypass pharmacotherapy and mechanical support.')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('2. **Surgery-Specific Focus:**')
    doc.append('   - Unlike outpatient diagnostic imaging, perioperative TEE is strictly goal-directed and procedure-specific. Echocardiographers must thoroughly master each technical surgical step, cannulation route, clamping sequence, and potential mechanical failure mode.')
    doc.append('   - Rapid and unambiguous communication between the echocardiographer, cardiac surgeon, and perfusionist is mandatory to ensure patient safety.')
    doc.append('')
    doc.append('3. **Comprehensive Coverage Across 11 Surgical Domains:**')
    doc.append('   - This guideline provides structured protocols for: (1) Mitral Valve Surgery, (2) Aortic Valve Surgery, (3) Tricuspid Valve Surgery, (4) Pulmonary Valve Surgery, (5) Coronary Artery Bypass Grafting (CABG), (6) Thoracic Aortic Surgery, (7) Mechanical Circulatory Support (LVAD, RVAD, BiVAD, TAH, ECMO, IABP), (8) Hypertrophic Cardiomyopathy (Septal Myectomy), (9) Orthotopic Heart Transplantation, (10) Lung Transplantation, and (11) Pericardial Diseases and Intracardiac Masses.')
